{"id": "mm7338a3", "status": "ok", "message_id": "msg_011Cgg9ucezEsBWYQKVjELL5", "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "errors": [], "usage": {"input": 33828, "output": 3765}, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "```json\n{\"id\": \"mm7338a3\",\n \"data_focus\": {\"v\": \"yes\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Estimated coverage with all recommended childhood vaccines was lower among children born in 2020 and 2021 than among those born in 2018 and 2019\"}]},\n \"outcome_types\": [{\"v\": \"binary/categorical\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"table 1\", \"q\": \"Estimated vaccination coverage, by age 24 months* among children born during 2018–2019 and 2020–2021\"}]}],\n \"analytic_depth\": [{\"v\": \"comparison\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Nationally and by jurisdiction, estimated coverage among children born in 2020 and 2021 was compared with estimated coverage among children born in 2018 and 2019.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"For data stratified by sociodemographic characteristics, subgroup estimates were compared with those for a designated referent group.\"}]}],\n \"study_design\": [\n   {\"v\": \"cross-sectional\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Children born during 2020–2021 were identified using data collected during 2021–2023\"}]},\n   {\"v\": \"before/after or trend\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"This report assesses trends in vaccination coverage by year of birth\"}]},\n   {\"v\": \"evaluation or monitoring\", \"ev\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"but the objectives for ≥1 dose of MMR (≥90.8%) and ≥4 doses of DTaP (≥90.0%) have not\"}]}\n ],\n \"methods_quotes\": [\n   {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Differences in coverage estimates were evaluated using z-tests at an α-level of 0.05.\"},\n   {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"for most vaccines, Kaplan-Meier techniques were used to estimate coverage by age 24 months\"},\n   {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"For data stratified by sociodemographic characteristics, subgroup estimates were compared with those for a designated referent group.\"},\n   {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Analyses used weighted data and were performed using SAS software (version 9.4; SAS Institute) and SUDAAN software (version 11; RTI International).\"},\n   {\"loc\": \"table 2\", \"q\": \"Estimate not available because the unweighted sample size for the denominator was <30\"}\n ],\n \"confidence\": \"high\",\n \"uncertain_fields\": [\"study_design\"]}\n```", "type": "text"}]}